\newlabel{fig:confusion_matrices}{{5}{17}{Confusion matrices for all seven models arranged in a 4×2 layout, showing the distribution of predicted versus actual class assignments. AHFS-TA achieves the highest diagonal concentrations (262 Dropout, 140 Enrolled, 429 Graduate correctly classified), indicating superior classification performance across all three classes. Notably, AHFS-TA dramatically reduces misclassification of the challenging Enrolled class, which poses difficulties for all baseline models due to its smaller sample size and inherent ambiguity}{figure.caption.12}{}}
